1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:30,000
= kissasia.net =

2
00:00:21,380 --> 00:00:23,940
♪Her smile, her kindness, her kiss♪

3
00:00:24,020 --> 00:00:25,820
♪Her presumptions♪

4
00:00:27,740 --> 00:00:30,300
♪She was in love, she was tired, she walked away♪

5
00:00:30,300 --> 00:00:32,660
♪Only tears remained♪

6
00:00:34,260 --> 00:00:36,180
♪Can't hold on, can't forget♪

7
00:00:36,340 --> 00:00:39,500
♪Can't let go of her all-or-nothing love♪

8
00:00:40,940 --> 00:00:44,100
♪Promises became a burden after all that hesitation♪

9
00:00:44,340 --> 00:00:47,500
♪Leaving longing frozen into a winter night♪

10
00:00:48,060 --> 00:00:53,420
♪That girl, my girl♪

11
00:00:54,340 --> 00:00:57,540
♪The light's still on, but you're already far away♪

12
00:00:57,780 --> 00:01:01,020
♪The words reach my lips, but I can't get them out♪

13
00:01:01,380 --> 00:01:06,740
♪That girl, my girl♪

14
00:01:07,620 --> 00:01:10,860
♪My voice echoes, but no one answers♪

15
00:01:11,100 --> 00:01:14,340
♪Is this really how it ends for us?♪

16
00:01:31,100 --> 00:01:33,980
[You don't have to be perfect tobe worthy of Love]

17
00:01:34,020 --> 00:01:35,380
[The Early Spring]

18
00:01:35,380 --> 00:01:37,940
[Adapted from The Early Spring on jjwxc.net, Author: Gu Niang Bie Ku]

19
00:01:48,510 --> 00:01:49,400
Is that him?

20
00:01:50,680 --> 00:01:51,430
That's him.

21
00:01:52,480 --> 00:01:53,840
I've seen his picture.

22
00:01:53,950 --> 00:01:55,240
He sure looks decent.

23
00:01:55,240 --> 00:01:55,950
That's him.

24
00:01:55,950 --> 00:01:57,480
Anyone who bullies our daughter is no better than a dog.

25
00:01:57,590 --> 00:01:58,920
I'm going to have a word with him.

26
00:02:00,120 --> 00:02:00,870
Come back.

27
00:02:00,870 --> 00:02:01,430
What's wrong?

28
00:02:01,430 --> 00:02:03,000
What are you doing?

29
00:02:03,510 --> 00:02:04,710
Tao isn't back yet.

30
00:02:04,710 --> 00:02:05,920
You're not young anymore.

31
00:02:05,920 --> 00:02:07,640
Trying to pick a fight with him?

32
00:02:07,640 --> 00:02:08,560
Honestly.

33
00:02:08,560 --> 00:02:09,910
Doesn't he get under your skin?

34
00:02:10,400 --> 00:02:11,870
Keep it down.

35
00:02:11,960 --> 00:02:13,190
Why should we serve him?

36
00:02:13,190 --> 00:02:14,430
Why feed him?

37
00:02:14,630 --> 00:02:15,560
You're treating him like our son-in-law now.

38
00:02:15,560 --> 00:02:17,470
I didn't serve him.

39
00:02:17,470 --> 00:02:19,240
I didn't even bring out the dishes he ordered.

40
00:02:19,440 --> 00:02:21,950
He helped himself to the peanuts

41
00:02:21,950 --> 00:02:24,110
and the drinks.

42
00:02:24,110 --> 00:02:25,830
Was I supposed to stop him from drinking?

43
00:02:25,830 --> 00:02:26,830
Jeez.

44
00:02:26,830 --> 00:02:28,350
Boss, bill, please.

45
00:02:28,350 --> 00:02:29,070
Coming.

46
00:02:30,280 --> 00:02:30,950
Here you go.

47
00:02:31,630 --> 00:02:32,280
That'll be 150.

48
00:02:36,550 --> 00:02:37,350
Tao,

49
00:02:37,550 --> 00:02:38,630
where are you?

50
00:02:39,000 --> 00:02:40,280
Hurry home.

51
00:02:40,280 --> 00:02:41,200
Thank you.

52
00:02:41,440 --> 00:02:42,400
Alright. See you.

53
00:02:57,040 --> 00:02:58,350
We're closed.

54
00:03:01,830 --> 00:03:02,440
Mr. Shang,

55
00:03:03,280 --> 00:03:04,160
it's only eight.

56
00:03:04,830 --> 00:03:06,040
The sign says you close at ten.

57
00:03:06,280 --> 00:03:07,670
Don't call me that.

58
00:03:08,110 --> 00:03:09,480
I own this place.

59
00:03:09,720 --> 00:03:11,630
I'll close whenever I want.

60
00:03:12,280 --> 00:03:12,830
Mr. Shang,

61
00:03:13,480 --> 00:03:14,200
I'm waiting for someone.

62
00:03:14,720 --> 00:03:16,350
I told you not to call me that.

63
00:03:17,040 --> 00:03:17,830
Listen.

64
00:03:18,110 --> 00:03:19,950
Stop wasting your time.

65
00:03:20,630 --> 00:03:22,040
The person you're waiting for is not coming today.

66
00:03:22,760 --> 00:03:23,510
How about this?

67
00:03:24,110 --> 00:03:25,320
You and Mrs. Shang go upstairs first.

68
00:03:25,510 --> 00:03:26,320
I'll mind the shop.

69
00:03:26,760 --> 00:03:27,630
I'm not leaving

70
00:03:27,630 --> 00:03:28,230
until Tao comes back.

71
00:03:28,720 --> 00:03:30,320
Who says you can call her "Tao"?

72
00:03:36,860 --> 00:03:40,540
[Episode 23]
[Luke Is My Dog Too]

73
00:03:42,830 --> 00:03:44,550
Who says you can call her "Tao"?

74
00:03:53,670 --> 00:03:54,480
You're back.

75
00:03:56,070 --> 00:03:56,670
Dad,

76
00:03:57,440 --> 00:03:58,480
I'll close up tonight.

77
00:03:58,480 --> 00:03:59,510
You two go upstairs.

78
00:04:00,390 --> 00:04:01,000
Don't worry.

79
00:04:10,040 --> 00:04:10,480
In that case,

80
00:04:11,230 --> 00:04:12,160
take care of yourself.

81
00:04:45,550 --> 00:04:46,310
Mr. Luan,

82
00:04:46,990 --> 00:04:48,520
our tavern is tiny.

83
00:04:49,400 --> 00:04:50,750
Why don't you grab a drink somewhere else?

84
00:04:51,990 --> 00:04:53,310
Let's talk somewhere else.

85
00:04:53,600 --> 00:04:54,280
No need.

86
00:04:57,480 --> 00:04:59,400
If you want to discuss work, come to the office.

87
00:04:59,840 --> 00:05:00,670
There's nothing to talk about

88
00:05:01,670 --> 00:05:02,920
here.

89
00:05:07,080 --> 00:05:08,110
You've always held a grudge against me.

90
00:05:13,080 --> 00:05:14,190
How could I?

91
00:05:14,190 --> 00:05:15,080
You're

92
00:05:16,190 --> 00:05:17,720
such a big shot.

93
00:05:18,840 --> 00:05:20,280
Why would I hold a grudge?

94
00:05:26,960 --> 00:05:27,600
Tao.

95
00:05:29,480 --> 00:05:30,790
Can you please talk to me nicely?

96
00:05:31,840 --> 00:05:33,670
It's not that I can't.

97
00:05:36,160 --> 00:05:38,350
I just don't have anything to say to you.

98
00:06:08,040 --> 00:06:10,990
You've received 10,000 yuan via Alipay.

99
00:06:15,520 --> 00:06:16,310
Luan Nian.

100
00:06:19,110 --> 00:06:20,670
It's only one plate of peanuts and one bottle of soda.

101
00:06:20,670 --> 00:06:21,750
Why did you pay ten thousand?

102
00:06:22,040 --> 00:06:22,670
If you're that rich,

103
00:06:22,670 --> 00:06:24,040
why don't you just buy this tavern?

104
00:06:26,160 --> 00:06:27,280
Would you sell it?

105
00:06:29,190 --> 00:06:30,840
Everything has a price in your eyes.

106
00:06:32,160 --> 00:06:32,550
Why did you sell

107
00:06:32,550 --> 00:06:34,040
the bags and gifts I gave you?

108
00:06:38,400 --> 00:06:39,670
If it's because

109
00:06:40,040 --> 00:06:41,310
I sold your gifts

110
00:06:41,640 --> 00:06:43,160
and left without saying goodbye,

111
00:06:43,350 --> 00:06:44,600
I'll apologize.

112
00:06:45,960 --> 00:06:47,920
I haven't spent a single cent from selling those bags.

113
00:06:47,920 --> 00:06:48,600
If you want it back,

114
00:06:48,600 --> 00:06:50,040
give me your account number.

115
00:06:50,790 --> 00:06:51,790
I'll transfer the money back.

116
00:06:52,080 --> 00:06:53,230
If you don't,

117
00:06:53,400 --> 00:06:54,920
I'll donate it when I get the chance.

118
00:06:54,920 --> 00:06:55,750
How does that sound?

119
00:06:59,790 --> 00:07:00,600
Keep it.

120
00:07:05,550 --> 00:07:06,280
Alright.

121
00:07:08,110 --> 00:07:09,080
I'll keep it.

122
00:07:10,960 --> 00:07:12,040
Now we're even.

123
00:07:15,230 --> 00:07:15,960
Shang Zhitao.

124
00:07:20,920 --> 00:07:21,920
I'll come back tomorrow.

125
00:07:22,670 --> 00:07:24,080
What exactly do you want?

126
00:07:26,350 --> 00:07:27,750
You want to tell my parents about what happened between us,

127
00:07:27,750 --> 00:07:29,190
don't you?

128
00:07:29,480 --> 00:07:30,840
You don't have to.

129
00:07:31,040 --> 00:07:32,600
I'll tell them right now.

130
00:07:32,600 --> 00:07:34,750
I behaved badly.

131
00:07:35,110 --> 00:07:36,110
I got involved with you

132
00:07:36,310 --> 00:07:37,670
because I wanted to climb the ladder.

133
00:07:42,280 --> 00:07:43,230
I've never thought of our relationship

134
00:07:43,230 --> 00:07:44,230
that way.

135
00:07:45,280 --> 00:07:46,160
Shang Zhitao,

136
00:07:47,720 --> 00:07:49,520
I truly loved you during those six years.

137
00:07:53,870 --> 00:07:54,790
That doesn't matter anymore.

138
00:07:57,840 --> 00:07:59,350
We're over.

139
00:08:10,920 --> 00:08:11,720
Luan Nian,

140
00:08:13,790 --> 00:08:15,080
I'm really tired.

141
00:08:19,110 --> 00:08:19,990
I've barely slept for two days

142
00:08:19,990 --> 00:08:21,600
because of this summit.

143
00:08:25,310 --> 00:08:26,640
Can I drive you home?

144
00:08:27,720 --> 00:08:29,040
When you're exhausted,

145
00:08:29,110 --> 00:08:30,280
driving is dangerous.

146
00:08:38,420 --> 00:08:40,220
[Old Couple's Tavern]

147
00:08:54,830 --> 00:08:56,120
Follow the GPS.

148
00:09:12,640 --> 00:09:14,880
Today's high in Harbin is minus thirteen degrees.

149
00:09:14,880 --> 00:09:17,040
The low is minus twenty-two degrees.

150
00:09:17,040 --> 00:09:17,880
It's bitterly cold

151
00:09:17,880 --> 00:09:18,920
and humid.

152
00:09:18,920 --> 00:09:20,240
Bundle up

153
00:09:20,240 --> 00:09:21,640
to keep from getting sick.

154
00:09:27,220 --> 00:09:30,500
♪One look is all it takes to find the right person♪

155
00:09:30,700 --> 00:09:33,060
♪One lifetime is all it takes to commemorate this love♪

156
00:09:34,300 --> 00:09:38,140
♪Whatever remains will be the proof♪

157
00:09:41,500 --> 00:09:44,980
♪If it never crosses your mind♪

158
00:09:45,100 --> 00:09:48,620
♪The tide as I turn back♪

159
00:09:48,860 --> 00:09:52,700
♪Is just formless attraction♪

160
00:09:54,780 --> 00:09:59,860
♪Your silhouette is closing in♪

161
00:10:01,980 --> 00:10:07,100
♪Your breathing grows clear♪

162
00:10:08,940 --> 00:10:13,260
♪Too many distractions in this world♪

163
00:10:13,420 --> 00:10:17,500
♪I would rather forget myself♪

164
00:10:17,780 --> 00:10:21,820
♪Just this moment♪

165
00:11:10,040 --> 00:11:11,190
I'm home.

166
00:11:11,950 --> 00:11:13,430
I'll come get it from you tomorrow.

167
00:11:14,470 --> 00:11:15,470
No need to pick me up.

168
00:11:15,670 --> 00:11:16,280
Okay.

169
00:11:17,760 --> 00:11:18,640
See you tomorrow.

170
00:11:44,040 --> 00:11:45,160
How are you getting back?

171
00:11:47,120 --> 00:11:47,670
It's okay.

172
00:11:48,640 --> 00:11:49,550
I can get back by myself.

173
00:11:51,470 --> 00:11:52,190
Thanks.

174
00:13:05,620 --> 00:13:06,590
[Lumi]

175
00:13:06,590 --> 00:13:09,070
Mr. Luan seems to have taken quite a blow.

176
00:13:09,430 --> 00:13:10,920
He suddenly disappeared.

177
00:13:11,640 --> 00:13:13,310
Are you two together?

178
00:14:19,590 --> 00:14:20,310
Luan Nian,

179
00:14:20,470 --> 00:14:21,270
have you lost your mind?

180
00:14:21,270 --> 00:14:22,400
What are you doing out here?

181
00:14:25,470 --> 00:14:26,520
It's freezing.

182
00:14:28,040 --> 00:14:28,710
I thought I'd have a drink

183
00:14:29,550 --> 00:14:30,360
to warm up.

184
00:14:31,920 --> 00:14:33,430
Are you trying to freeze to death?

185
00:14:33,550 --> 00:14:35,190
Do you think I'd take responsibility if something happened to you?

186
00:14:37,520 --> 00:14:38,470
Would you?

187
00:14:38,710 --> 00:14:39,430
No.

188
00:14:52,120 --> 00:14:53,520
Do you have a boyfriend now?

189
00:14:54,190 --> 00:14:55,190
What are you talking about?

190
00:14:59,830 --> 00:15:01,790
I heard your assistant call that guy brother-in-law.

191
00:15:04,240 --> 00:15:05,430
He's not my boyfriend.

192
00:15:06,830 --> 00:15:07,830
He's my fiancé.

193
00:15:25,550 --> 00:15:26,640
Is Luke still alive?

194
00:15:27,590 --> 00:15:28,520
Luke's still young.

195
00:15:28,520 --> 00:15:29,640
Why wouldn't he be?

196
00:15:29,830 --> 00:15:30,670
Is he at home?

197
00:15:31,520 --> 00:15:32,280
Yeah.

198
00:15:34,120 --> 00:15:35,060
I want to see him.

199
00:15:35,060 --> 00:15:36,980
♪Still can't define♪

200
00:15:38,360 --> 00:15:39,640
I don't want Luke to see you.

201
00:15:39,640 --> 00:15:40,920
He'd be heartbroken.

202
00:15:44,920 --> 00:15:46,120
Even Luke misses me.

203
00:15:47,920 --> 00:15:48,660
You're worse than a dog.

204
00:15:48,660 --> 00:15:52,100
♪That you only see clearly up close...♪

205
00:15:52,470 --> 00:15:53,360
Luan Nian.

206
00:15:55,670 --> 00:15:57,830
We've been tangled up for so many years.

207
00:15:57,830 --> 00:15:59,070
I'm exhausted.

208
00:16:00,920 --> 00:16:02,190
Now,

209
00:16:02,880 --> 00:16:04,760
I just want to live my own life,

210
00:16:05,430 --> 00:16:06,790
take care of my family,

211
00:16:07,120 --> 00:16:09,550
and put my life back in order.

212
00:16:11,040 --> 00:16:12,550
I don't want anything else.

213
00:16:13,950 --> 00:16:15,240
If you have to know

214
00:16:15,240 --> 00:16:17,070
why I left without saying goodbye,

215
00:16:17,880 --> 00:16:19,070
it's because I knew

216
00:16:19,070 --> 00:16:20,470
if I'd said goodbye,

217
00:16:20,470 --> 00:16:22,790
you would've said a lot of hurtful things.

218
00:16:22,790 --> 00:16:24,310
I'd had enough of that.

219
00:16:34,310 --> 00:16:35,240
Finished?

220
00:16:36,310 --> 00:16:37,240
Yeah.

221
00:16:38,640 --> 00:16:40,000
Then let me say a few things.

222
00:16:42,590 --> 00:16:43,310
Go ahead.

223
00:16:43,790 --> 00:16:45,040
There's something

224
00:16:45,040 --> 00:16:46,040
I think you deserve to hear from me.

225
00:16:47,830 --> 00:16:49,280
Back when you were up for the Specialist title,

226
00:16:50,120 --> 00:16:51,040
I gave you

227
00:16:51,880 --> 00:16:52,790
a very high score.

228
00:16:53,550 --> 00:16:55,710
I only found out afterward that Song Ying had been added as your competitor.

229
00:16:57,080 --> 00:16:58,430
You always told me to be fair.

230
00:16:59,430 --> 00:17:00,430
I was.

231
00:17:01,310 --> 00:17:03,240
My score reflected how I saw you.

232
00:17:04,080 --> 00:17:06,320
If you think you weren't good enough

233
00:17:06,670 --> 00:17:07,840
when you first joined Lime,

234
00:17:08,710 --> 00:17:09,750
that you lacked confidence,

235
00:17:10,670 --> 00:17:12,640
or that I looked down on you even when you left,

236
00:17:13,160 --> 00:17:14,640
then let me make one thing clear.

237
00:17:15,510 --> 00:17:17,270
When you first joined, you weren't very good.

238
00:17:18,560 --> 00:17:19,950
But by the time you left,

239
00:17:21,360 --> 00:17:22,840
you were the best employee I'd ever trained.

240
00:17:25,670 --> 00:17:27,030
It was snowing that day too.

241
00:17:28,080 --> 00:17:29,400
You walked out of my place.

242
00:17:30,750 --> 00:17:32,880
You made Luke choose between you and me.

243
00:17:36,510 --> 00:17:38,670
It felt like getting divorced.

244
00:17:40,230 --> 00:17:42,080
At least people negotiate during a divorce.

245
00:17:42,360 --> 00:17:42,990
But you?

246
00:17:43,800 --> 00:17:45,320
You just walked away.

247
00:17:47,800 --> 00:17:48,560
Did you think you were the only one

248
00:17:48,560 --> 00:17:49,920
who gave your heart over the past six years?

249
00:17:51,120 --> 00:17:52,270
What about mine?

250
00:17:54,270 --> 00:17:55,670
Didn't I try?

251
00:17:55,980 --> 00:17:59,460
♪Love is tears, and the more they overflow, the sadder it becomes♪

252
00:17:59,540 --> 00:18:03,740
♪Once the rainy season passes, I'll decide who to forget...♪

253
00:18:06,710 --> 00:18:07,510
Luan Nian.

254
00:18:11,840 --> 00:18:13,400
I'm really grateful

255
00:18:13,400 --> 00:18:15,400
for everything you've done for me over those years.

256
00:18:16,320 --> 00:18:17,800
I truly appreciate it.

257
00:18:19,320 --> 00:18:20,320
I already wished you well

258
00:18:20,320 --> 00:18:21,560
in the last message

259
00:18:21,560 --> 00:18:23,320
I sent you.

260
00:18:28,670 --> 00:18:30,990
I always hope everything goes well for you.

261
00:18:34,120 --> 00:18:35,400
But

262
00:18:38,360 --> 00:18:40,670
we still have a long life ahead of us.

263
00:18:43,640 --> 00:18:46,160
There are so many things worth doing

264
00:18:46,320 --> 00:18:48,640
and so many people worth loving.

265
00:18:55,800 --> 00:18:57,430
Go back, Luan Nian.

266
00:19:00,360 --> 00:19:01,190
I'm not leaving.

267
00:19:02,750 --> 00:19:04,320
I want to see Luke right now.

268
00:19:06,080 --> 00:19:08,030
Luke had been with me since the day we brought him home.

269
00:19:08,670 --> 00:19:09,840
I fed him.

270
00:19:10,080 --> 00:19:11,030
I took him hiking.

271
00:19:11,030 --> 00:19:11,800
I walked him.

272
00:19:12,160 --> 00:19:13,840
Why can't I see him?

273
00:19:14,120 --> 00:19:15,560
Because Luke is my dog.

274
00:19:15,560 --> 00:19:16,940
Your dog's name is Luke.

275
00:19:18,320 --> 00:19:20,320
He's named after my English name.

276
00:19:26,230 --> 00:19:27,270
I trained him too.

277
00:19:27,270 --> 00:19:28,670
Why can't I see him?

278
00:19:31,180 --> 00:19:32,820
♪Her smile, her kindness♪

279
00:19:32,900 --> 00:19:36,100
♪Her kiss, her presumptions♪

280
00:19:37,820 --> 00:19:39,460
♪She was in love, she was tired♪

281
00:19:39,540 --> 00:19:42,420
♪She walked away, only tears remained♪

282
00:19:44,460 --> 00:19:46,900
♪I can't describe, hear, or find♪

283
00:19:46,980 --> 00:19:48,900
♪Her candor♪

284
00:19:50,900 --> 00:19:53,740
♪Silence replaces the words that pass down my judgment♪

285
00:19:54,260 --> 00:19:57,340
♪Let our memories be void♪

286
00:19:57,900 --> 00:19:59,460
♪Her fear, her pain♪

287
00:19:59,540 --> 00:20:02,620
♪Her dreams, the way she pulls away♪

288
00:20:04,300 --> 00:20:05,980
♪I care, I understand♪

289
00:20:06,060 --> 00:20:09,100
♪Why are we left in such a mess?♪

290
00:20:11,020 --> 00:20:13,540
♪Can't hold on, can't forget, can't let go♪

291
00:20:13,700 --> 00:20:15,780
♪Of her all-or-nothing love...♪

292
00:20:16,670 --> 00:20:17,360
Tao.

293
00:20:17,740 --> 00:20:20,900
♪Promises became a burden after all that hesitation♪

294
00:20:21,020 --> 00:20:23,900
♪Leaving longing frozen into a winter night♪

295
00:20:24,500 --> 00:20:28,740
♪That girl, my girl...♪

296
00:20:28,750 --> 00:20:30,600
You just want to see Luke?

297
00:20:30,980 --> 00:20:33,700
♪The light's still on, but you're already far away...♪

298
00:20:33,710 --> 00:20:34,320
Yes.

299
00:20:34,420 --> 00:20:36,980
♪The words reach my lips, but I can't get them out♪

300
00:20:38,080 --> 00:20:38,710
Okay.

301
00:21:01,320 --> 00:21:02,030
Luke!

302
00:21:03,190 --> 00:21:03,800
Luke.

303
00:21:04,950 --> 00:21:05,640
Luke.

304
00:21:09,990 --> 00:21:11,230
Let me take a look at you. There, there.

305
00:21:13,400 --> 00:21:14,230
You've gotten thinner.

306
00:21:15,190 --> 00:21:16,510
She doesn't let you eat meat, does she?

307
00:21:17,510 --> 00:21:18,710
His stomach is sensitive.

308
00:21:19,190 --> 00:21:20,430
If he eats too much, he'll throw up.

309
00:21:23,230 --> 00:21:25,160
Looks like Mr. Xing hasn't been around much.

310
00:21:29,800 --> 00:21:31,160
You had a point.

311
00:21:34,470 --> 00:21:35,920
I shouldn't stop you

312
00:21:36,230 --> 00:21:37,640
from seeing Luke.

313
00:21:38,920 --> 00:21:40,600
After all, you raised him.

314
00:21:40,880 --> 00:21:42,640
If you miss him,

315
00:21:43,080 --> 00:21:44,320
just let me know.

316
00:21:44,800 --> 00:21:46,270
You can take him out anytime.

317
00:21:51,080 --> 00:21:52,320
I have a few more things to say.

318
00:21:55,270 --> 00:21:55,880
Go ahead.

319
00:21:58,710 --> 00:21:59,920
Don't transfer money to me anymore.

320
00:22:01,950 --> 00:22:04,640
When you do, it reminds me of

321
00:22:05,710 --> 00:22:06,670
how you used to buy me

322
00:22:07,080 --> 00:22:08,430
expensive bags.

323
00:22:09,840 --> 00:22:12,160
It makes me very, very uncomfortable.

324
00:22:14,510 --> 00:22:16,560
And don't use any excuses to see my parents.

325
00:22:17,800 --> 00:22:19,030
I don't like that.

326
00:22:21,470 --> 00:22:22,080
Alright.

327
00:22:22,640 --> 00:22:23,710
One more thing.

328
00:22:25,190 --> 00:22:26,880
Things are fine the way they are now.

329
00:22:27,360 --> 00:22:28,400
Let's leave it at that.

330
00:22:35,030 --> 00:22:35,670
Luke.

331
00:22:41,190 --> 00:22:42,080
I'm going now.

332
00:22:42,470 --> 00:22:43,320
I'll come see you again.

333
00:23:33,430 --> 00:23:34,360
Mr. Luan,

334
00:23:34,800 --> 00:23:35,840
what brings you here?

335
00:23:37,320 --> 00:23:37,710
Well,

336
00:23:37,710 --> 00:23:39,360
my boss stepped out.

337
00:23:40,600 --> 00:23:41,360
Please have a seat.

338
00:23:41,510 --> 00:23:42,470
I'll give her a call.

339
00:23:43,120 --> 00:23:43,710
No need.

340
00:23:44,270 --> 00:23:45,430
I was just passing by.

341
00:23:45,750 --> 00:23:46,470
I'll leave in a minute.

342
00:23:47,880 --> 00:23:48,510
Have a seat, please.

343
00:23:50,670 --> 00:23:51,670
Is this her desk?

344
00:23:51,670 --> 00:23:52,270
Yeah.

345
00:24:02,940 --> 00:24:04,860
[Supplier Contacts]

346
00:24:07,270 --> 00:24:07,990
You like Coffee.

347
00:24:08,400 --> 00:24:09,190
Iced Americano.

348
00:24:09,400 --> 00:24:09,920
One moment, please.

349
00:24:09,920 --> 00:24:10,710
I'll go buy one now.

350
00:24:11,120 --> 00:24:12,990
Who trained your staff on client reception?

351
00:24:13,470 --> 00:24:14,400
My boss.

352
00:24:14,710 --> 00:24:16,080
She always says,

353
00:24:16,080 --> 00:24:17,510
"Be tactful when you work,

354
00:24:17,510 --> 00:24:19,470
and never lose your principles."

355
00:24:19,750 --> 00:24:20,440
Anything but sleeping with clients

356
00:24:20,440 --> 00:24:21,230
is fine.

357
00:24:24,510 --> 00:24:26,160
No sleeping with clients? Did she really say that?

358
00:24:28,840 --> 00:24:29,840
No.

359
00:24:30,800 --> 00:24:32,560
I was trying to be funny.

360
00:24:33,600 --> 00:24:34,950
What she meant was,

361
00:24:34,950 --> 00:24:36,560
be observant and know what people need.

362
00:24:41,190 --> 00:24:42,360
How long have you worked here?

363
00:24:42,990 --> 00:24:44,560
Two years.

364
00:24:47,710 --> 00:24:48,920
Does your boss

365
00:24:48,920 --> 00:24:50,320
go on dates often?

366
00:24:53,030 --> 00:24:55,270
Go on dates?

367
00:24:55,840 --> 00:24:57,560
Not at all.

368
00:24:58,270 --> 00:25:00,120
We usually don't get off work until ten.

369
00:25:00,640 --> 00:25:01,840
She stays even later than we do.

370
00:25:02,160 --> 00:25:03,670
So I'd say no.

371
00:25:05,560 --> 00:25:06,400
Are you sure?

372
00:25:07,670 --> 00:25:08,470
I'm sure.

373
00:25:11,950 --> 00:25:12,600
Alright.

374
00:25:14,510 --> 00:25:16,030
The restroom is outside to your right.

375
00:25:16,800 --> 00:25:17,600
I'll get going.

376
00:25:17,640 --> 00:25:18,470
I'll visit again sometime.

377
00:25:20,750 --> 00:25:21,640
Take care, Mr. Luan.

378
00:25:29,360 --> 00:25:30,560
Dates?

379
00:25:31,230 --> 00:25:33,080
Why was he asking about that?

380
00:25:50,080 --> 00:25:50,880
Can I ask you something?

381
00:25:50,990 --> 00:25:52,270
What is it? You seem anxious.

382
00:25:52,840 --> 00:25:53,450
Are the advertising budgets

383
00:25:53,450 --> 00:25:55,120
for your clients' regional branches

384
00:25:55,230 --> 00:25:56,190
handled separately?

385
00:25:58,230 --> 00:26:00,320
That's usually the case.

386
00:26:00,320 --> 00:26:02,270
The budget is allocated to each regional office to manage on its own.

387
00:26:05,400 --> 00:26:05,990
A friend of mine

388
00:26:05,990 --> 00:26:07,560
runs an ad agency in Harbin.

389
00:26:08,120 --> 00:26:09,750
Send some budget their way and let them give it a shot.

390
00:26:11,270 --> 00:26:12,400
Let me put it this way.

391
00:26:12,920 --> 00:26:13,640
Every agency I've introduced to you

392
00:26:13,640 --> 00:26:14,990
does honest work.

393
00:26:14,990 --> 00:26:16,190
They're all solid teams.

394
00:26:18,470 --> 00:26:19,990
Say no more. I know.

395
00:26:20,470 --> 00:26:21,560
It's Shang Zhitao, right?

396
00:26:28,670 --> 00:26:29,600
I'll give you the contact.

397
00:26:29,600 --> 00:26:30,430
Get in touch with them yourself.

398
00:26:30,840 --> 00:26:31,750
The contact person is Fu Dong.

399
00:26:36,470 --> 00:26:37,560
You've been to Harbin

400
00:26:37,840 --> 00:26:39,320
so many times,

401
00:26:40,030 --> 00:26:41,080
and still got nowhere.

402
00:26:50,600 --> 00:26:52,080
Is Shang Zhitao married?

403
00:26:53,750 --> 00:26:54,750
None of your business.

404
00:26:57,430 --> 00:26:58,710
None of my business.

405
00:27:02,360 --> 00:27:03,120
That's satisfying.

406
00:27:03,320 --> 00:27:04,120
Never thought I'd live to see

407
00:27:04,120 --> 00:27:05,990
someone like you, who never listens to anyone,

408
00:27:05,990 --> 00:27:06,990
finally brought to heel.

409
00:27:07,230 --> 00:27:08,230
Are you done?

410
00:27:09,560 --> 00:27:10,360
Look,

411
00:27:10,360 --> 00:27:12,430
we're all rooting for you to win her back.

412
00:27:12,880 --> 00:27:14,230
But could you

413
00:27:14,230 --> 00:27:15,640
be a little more straightforward?

414
00:27:16,640 --> 00:27:18,600
If you love someone, just say it.

415
00:27:19,030 --> 00:27:20,320
Be sweet.

416
00:27:21,080 --> 00:27:22,030
Be gentle.

417
00:27:22,270 --> 00:27:23,400
See her often.

418
00:27:24,030 --> 00:27:25,190
Take it one step at a time.

419
00:27:25,190 --> 00:27:26,600
Don't rush it.

420
00:27:52,560 --> 00:27:53,360
Who is it?

421
00:27:55,670 --> 00:27:56,920
Why are you here again?

422
00:27:57,360 --> 00:27:58,320
I'm here to see Luke.

423
00:27:58,990 --> 00:28:00,320
Did you tell me in advance?

424
00:28:00,360 --> 00:28:01,030
Luke.

425
00:28:01,880 --> 00:28:02,670
Luke.

426
00:28:05,120 --> 00:28:05,710
Look

427
00:28:06,120 --> 00:28:06,950
what I brought.

428
00:28:07,400 --> 00:28:08,320
I bought meat.

429
00:28:08,560 --> 00:28:10,160
I'll make you some meatballs later.

430
00:28:10,160 --> 00:28:10,950
You need to fatten up.

431
00:28:10,950 --> 00:28:11,400
Good boy.

432
00:28:18,190 --> 00:28:19,120
Let's go, Luke.

433
00:28:21,270 --> 00:28:21,800
Come on.

434
00:28:22,800 --> 00:28:23,750
Luke.

435
00:28:30,750 --> 00:28:31,750
Luke.

436
00:28:34,710 --> 00:28:35,710
Luke.

437
00:28:36,360 --> 00:28:37,560
Look at you drooling.

438
00:28:38,320 --> 00:28:39,400
I'll make them for you later.

439
00:28:42,640 --> 00:28:44,600
I ran into your neighbor downstairs earlier today.

440
00:28:45,120 --> 00:28:46,710
She asked if I was your boyfriend.

441
00:28:49,880 --> 00:28:50,950
And?

442
00:28:52,230 --> 00:28:53,160
I said yes.

443
00:28:56,030 --> 00:28:56,920
It's fine.

444
00:28:56,920 --> 00:28:58,320
My reputation is bad anyway.

445
00:29:00,800 --> 00:29:02,080
That's a relief.

446
00:29:02,400 --> 00:29:03,750
Mine isn't great either.

447
00:29:04,160 --> 00:29:05,750
Two jerks. Perfect match.

448
00:29:08,360 --> 00:29:09,190
Luke,

449
00:29:09,750 --> 00:29:11,840
did you hear what he said?

450
00:29:12,160 --> 00:29:13,990
How about we poison him so he can't talk anymore?

451
00:29:50,860 --> 00:29:54,180
♪One look is all it takes to find the right person♪

452
00:29:54,260 --> 00:29:56,700
♪One lifetime is all it takes to commemorate this love♪

453
00:29:57,900 --> 00:30:01,740
♪Whatever remains will be the proof♪

454
00:30:05,180 --> 00:30:08,620
♪If it never crosses your mind♪

455
00:30:08,740 --> 00:30:12,300
♪The tide as I turn back♪

456
00:30:12,500 --> 00:30:16,340
♪Is just formless attraction♪

457
00:30:18,500 --> 00:30:23,540
♪Your silhouette is closing in♪

458
00:30:25,580 --> 00:30:30,740
♪Your breathing grows clear♪

459
00:30:32,620 --> 00:30:36,980
♪Too many distractions in this world♪

460
00:30:37,020 --> 00:30:41,180
♪I would rather forget myself♪

461
00:30:41,460 --> 00:30:45,380
♪Just this moment♪

462
00:30:47,400 --> 00:30:48,190
Tao.

463
00:30:49,470 --> 00:30:50,270
Tao.

464
00:30:51,670 --> 00:30:52,560
Mom.

465
00:30:52,640 --> 00:30:53,320
Dad.

466
00:30:54,030 --> 00:30:55,640
Why are you here?

467
00:30:55,640 --> 00:30:57,920
There weren't many customers today.

468
00:30:57,920 --> 00:30:58,880
Your dad said

469
00:30:58,880 --> 00:31:00,560
we'd bring you some food.

470
00:31:03,510 --> 00:31:05,190
What's wrong?

471
00:31:06,030 --> 00:31:07,230
Can't we come?

472
00:31:07,230 --> 00:31:08,030
Look at this girl.

473
00:31:08,030 --> 00:31:08,840
Well, well.

474
00:31:08,950 --> 00:31:09,360
Honestly.

475
00:31:09,360 --> 00:31:10,710
Dad, Mom.

476
00:31:12,120 --> 00:31:13,230
Mr. and Mrs. Shang, you are here.

477
00:31:14,990 --> 00:31:15,640
Mr. and Mrs. Shang.

478
00:31:16,880 --> 00:31:18,120
You have a guest?

479
00:31:20,600 --> 00:31:21,920
What is he doing here?

480
00:31:23,030 --> 00:31:24,160
Uh, he...

481
00:31:25,670 --> 00:31:26,750
Well.

482
00:31:26,920 --> 00:31:28,690
Luke has been sick,

483
00:31:28,690 --> 00:31:30,640
so he came to take care of him.

484
00:31:31,800 --> 00:31:32,320
That's right.

485
00:31:32,990 --> 00:31:33,840
Tao is busy,

486
00:31:34,160 --> 00:31:35,400
so I'm helping look after Luke.

487
00:31:39,920 --> 00:31:41,560
Are you cooking?

488
00:31:43,430 --> 00:31:44,670
Perfect timing.

489
00:31:45,030 --> 00:31:46,430
Let's stay and eat together.

490
00:31:47,080 --> 00:31:48,510
We've got guests.

491
00:31:48,510 --> 00:31:49,640
Don't just stand there.

492
00:31:49,640 --> 00:31:51,320
Lend him a hand.

493
00:31:51,510 --> 00:31:52,600
Help with what?

494
00:31:52,710 --> 00:31:53,660
I'm here to eat,

495
00:31:53,660 --> 00:31:54,750
not to work.

496
00:32:03,230 --> 00:32:03,990
Well.

497
00:32:03,990 --> 00:32:04,880
Luan...

498
00:32:05,470 --> 00:32:06,230
Luan Nian.

499
00:32:07,360 --> 00:32:08,230
Want a drink?

500
00:32:09,190 --> 00:32:10,430
Sure. I'll have a drink with you.

501
00:32:10,430 --> 00:32:10,990
Come.

502
00:32:14,080 --> 00:32:15,800
The first toast

503
00:32:15,800 --> 00:32:17,320
is for you.

504
00:32:17,320 --> 00:32:18,950
Welcome to Harbin.

505
00:32:19,670 --> 00:32:20,880
Thank you, Mr. Shang.

506
00:32:27,230 --> 00:32:28,320
The second toast.

507
00:32:29,120 --> 00:32:30,190
Thank you

508
00:32:30,560 --> 00:32:32,360
for supporting our tavern last time.

509
00:32:33,030 --> 00:32:33,750
My pleasure.

510
00:32:38,840 --> 00:32:40,400
Not eating the dishes?

511
00:32:40,400 --> 00:32:41,990
The third toast.

512
00:32:41,990 --> 00:32:42,920
Thank you

513
00:32:43,990 --> 00:32:46,080
and your friends for looking after her

514
00:32:46,080 --> 00:32:49,080
when Tao was all alone in Beijing.

515
00:32:50,320 --> 00:32:51,030
Come on.

516
00:32:53,400 --> 00:32:54,430
Have a bite.

517
00:32:54,430 --> 00:32:55,080
Soak up the alcohol.

518
00:32:55,080 --> 00:32:55,800
Eat the dishes.

519
00:32:55,800 --> 00:32:56,230
Here.

520
00:32:56,230 --> 00:32:57,880
Also, thank you

521
00:32:57,880 --> 00:32:59,470
for taking care of Luke.

522
00:33:00,080 --> 00:33:01,920
Are you sure you want to continue?

523
00:33:02,670 --> 00:33:04,400
Don't worry. He's a young man.

524
00:33:04,800 --> 00:33:05,710
Well.

525
00:33:08,230 --> 00:33:08,950
That's enough.

526
00:33:09,430 --> 00:33:10,560
At least eat something.

527
00:33:18,990 --> 00:33:20,160
Here. Drink it.

528
00:33:20,670 --> 00:33:21,320
Sure.

529
00:33:23,190 --> 00:33:24,030
Thank you.

530
00:33:24,030 --> 00:33:25,400
Are you hiding something from me?

531
00:33:25,400 --> 00:33:26,270
You looked after Luke well.

532
00:33:27,160 --> 00:33:27,710
I'm not.

533
00:33:27,710 --> 00:33:29,120
Wishing Luke good health as he grows up.

534
00:33:29,600 --> 00:33:31,190
You're hiding something from your mom.

535
00:33:31,190 --> 00:33:32,600
Don't interrupt.

536
00:33:33,670 --> 00:33:34,950
Listen to me.

537
00:33:35,640 --> 00:33:36,320
You...

538
00:33:36,320 --> 00:33:36,990
You...

539
00:33:37,950 --> 00:33:39,270
Have you thought this through?

540
00:33:39,470 --> 00:33:41,360
I'm always on your side.

541
00:33:41,990 --> 00:33:43,560
I'm really not hiding anything.

542
00:33:45,080 --> 00:33:47,560
A spoiled child never turns out well.

543
00:33:48,270 --> 00:33:50,160
You're definitely hiding something from me.

544
00:33:50,160 --> 00:33:51,160
That's the last.

545
00:33:51,670 --> 00:33:52,360
Come on.

546
00:33:52,360 --> 00:33:53,670
Don't let him drink anymore.

547
00:33:54,560 --> 00:33:56,320
Luke is closer to you

548
00:33:57,080 --> 00:33:58,230
than he is to Tao.

549
00:33:58,800 --> 00:33:59,430
Drink up.

550
00:33:59,510 --> 00:34:00,800
Stop drinking, Dad.

551
00:34:00,840 --> 00:34:01,840
- He can drink himself. - Shang.

552
00:34:01,840 --> 00:34:02,810
- Shang, stop it. - Cheers.

553
00:34:02,840 --> 00:34:03,430
No.

554
00:34:03,430 --> 00:34:04,430
He's drunk enough.

555
00:34:04,430 --> 00:34:05,160
I'll finish it.

556
00:34:05,160 --> 00:34:06,230
Don't drink anymore.

557
00:34:10,030 --> 00:34:10,800
Lan.

558
00:34:10,800 --> 00:34:11,950
Lan is not his name.

559
00:34:12,240 --> 00:34:13,170
It's Luan.

560
00:34:13,550 --> 00:34:14,550
Not Lan.

561
00:34:14,550 --> 00:34:15,990
- Luan. - Yes, I'm Luan.

562
00:34:16,070 --> 00:34:17,550
Mr. Shang, let's keep drinking.

563
00:34:17,550 --> 00:34:18,030
No.

564
00:34:18,030 --> 00:34:18,590
Let's drink some more.

565
00:34:19,550 --> 00:34:20,030
Stop it.

566
00:34:20,030 --> 00:34:20,500
That's enough.

567
00:34:20,500 --> 00:34:20,960
Don't.

568
00:34:20,960 --> 00:34:22,430
My daughter needs to rest.

569
00:34:22,430 --> 00:34:23,590
Which hotel are you staying at?

570
00:34:23,590 --> 00:34:24,680
Not drinking anymore?

571
00:34:28,590 --> 00:34:29,630
Where's he staying?

572
00:34:29,800 --> 00:34:30,320
How would I know?

573
00:34:30,320 --> 00:34:31,430
The room next door?

574
00:34:31,550 --> 00:34:33,070
I asked which hotel.

575
00:34:33,070 --> 00:34:34,840
I'm staying at the hotel next door, Mrs. Shang.

576
00:34:35,280 --> 00:34:36,720
Alright. Let's go.

577
00:34:36,720 --> 00:34:37,720
We'll leave together.

578
00:34:38,430 --> 00:34:39,200
Not drinking anymore?

579
00:34:39,360 --> 00:34:40,200
Are you leaving already?

580
00:34:40,200 --> 00:34:41,110
Easy there.

581
00:34:43,360 --> 00:34:43,990
Young man.

582
00:34:44,110 --> 00:34:45,320
- Young man, wait.
- That's not the door.

583
00:34:45,320 --> 00:34:46,200
That's not the door.

584
00:34:46,200 --> 00:34:48,200
He's a lightweight.

585
00:34:48,760 --> 00:34:49,510
Easy.

586
00:34:49,510 --> 00:34:49,920
I'm fine.

587
00:34:49,920 --> 00:34:50,680
I can walk by myself.

588
00:34:50,680 --> 00:34:52,150
Don't throw my dad's back out.

589
00:34:52,150 --> 00:34:52,990
Walk by yourself.

590
00:34:52,990 --> 00:34:54,200
- Go on. - Let him walk.

591
00:34:54,630 --> 00:34:55,430
Slow down.

592
00:34:55,430 --> 00:34:56,150
I'm fine.

593
00:34:56,280 --> 00:34:57,320
Easy.

594
00:34:58,150 --> 00:34:59,400
Can he make it?

595
00:34:59,400 --> 00:35:01,030
- Can he make it? - He's a young man.

596
00:35:01,470 --> 00:35:02,470
He holds his liquor well.

597
00:35:03,150 --> 00:35:04,510
He's well-mannered when he's drunk.

598
00:35:04,720 --> 00:35:05,110
You got him

599
00:35:05,110 --> 00:35:06,400
completely wasted.

600
00:35:06,400 --> 00:35:07,320
You poured him drink after drink.

601
00:35:07,320 --> 00:35:08,430
He didn't even have a bite to eat.

602
00:35:08,430 --> 00:35:10,030
The way someone acts when they're drunk says a lot about them.

603
00:35:10,200 --> 00:35:11,950
At least this trip wasn't for nothing.

604
00:35:13,110 --> 00:35:13,880
Alright.

605
00:35:13,880 --> 00:35:14,840
Go get some rest.

606
00:35:15,150 --> 00:35:15,950
Go to bed early.

607
00:35:17,880 --> 00:35:18,840
- Luan. - Bye.

608
00:35:18,920 --> 00:35:19,550
Wait.

609
00:35:19,600 --> 00:35:21,030
Let's go together.

610
00:35:21,030 --> 00:35:21,920
Easy now.

611
00:35:22,140 --> 00:35:24,110
- Come. - What's the rush?

612
00:35:51,590 --> 00:35:52,920
Why are you back?

613
00:35:54,510 --> 00:35:55,550
The hotel's fully booked.

614
00:35:55,590 --> 00:35:56,590
Excuse me.

615
00:36:00,400 --> 00:36:01,150
I have nowhere else to stay.

616
00:36:10,720 --> 00:36:12,200
Weren't you drunk?

617
00:36:13,680 --> 00:36:14,840
That wasn't enough to do it.

618
00:36:15,280 --> 00:36:16,200
You were faking.

619
00:36:18,280 --> 00:36:19,360
I'll take the guest room.

620
00:36:20,240 --> 00:36:21,680
Did I tell you to undress?

621
00:36:21,680 --> 00:36:23,030
Did I say yes?

622
00:36:25,760 --> 00:36:27,430
Knowing how hospitable people in Harbin are,

623
00:36:27,840 --> 00:36:29,510
you wouldn't leave me out on the street, would you?

624
00:36:30,240 --> 00:36:31,150
What exactly...

625
00:36:31,400 --> 00:36:32,150
Luan Nian.

626
00:36:34,630 --> 00:36:35,510
What do you want?

627
00:36:38,590 --> 00:36:39,920
I'll sleep on the couch if I have to.

628
00:36:48,630 --> 00:36:49,760
Suit yourself.

629
00:38:23,630 --> 00:38:24,430
Shang Zhitao,

630
00:38:26,400 --> 00:38:27,470
I know you're still awake.

631
00:38:28,840 --> 00:38:30,070
Just let me say a few things.

632
00:38:31,630 --> 00:38:32,550
You don't have to answer.

633
00:38:37,720 --> 00:38:38,600
After you left,

634
00:38:38,600 --> 00:38:40,150
I thought about us a lot.

635
00:38:42,840 --> 00:38:44,720
I know you put up with a lot

636
00:38:46,280 --> 00:38:47,550
in our relationship.

637
00:38:49,840 --> 00:38:51,840
You endured so much just to be with me,

638
00:38:52,070 --> 00:38:53,200
because you loved me.

639
00:38:57,550 --> 00:38:58,920
But back then,

640
00:39:00,030 --> 00:39:01,030
I was too arrogant.

641
00:39:02,720 --> 00:39:03,880
I realized everything too late.

642
00:39:05,950 --> 00:39:07,110
I didn't treat you well enough.

643
00:39:09,990 --> 00:39:11,590
But my feelings were real.

644
00:39:13,470 --> 00:39:14,720
I'm sure you could tell.

645
00:39:28,950 --> 00:39:30,240
When I said I wanted to take care of Luke with you,

646
00:39:30,240 --> 00:39:30,990
I meant it.

647
00:39:32,920 --> 00:39:34,070
We've still got a long road ahead.

648
00:39:35,550 --> 00:39:36,590
I'll take it one step at a time.

649
00:39:43,150 --> 00:39:43,990
Shang Zhitao,

650
00:39:46,880 --> 00:39:47,680
I'm sorry.

651
00:39:50,320 --> 00:39:51,590
For everything that happened.

652
00:40:17,800 --> 00:40:19,280
The old me always thought

653
00:40:20,680 --> 00:40:22,430
I wasn't good enough.

654
00:40:23,630 --> 00:40:25,150
Even so, I knew I was loved.

655
00:40:28,360 --> 00:40:29,550
We really did love each other.

656
00:40:31,030 --> 00:40:31,950
But

657
00:40:31,950 --> 00:40:33,150
he was too proud,

658
00:40:33,550 --> 00:40:34,880
and I was too insecure.

659
00:40:35,510 --> 00:40:36,470
Neither of us

660
00:40:36,920 --> 00:40:38,360
would back down.

661
00:40:40,200 --> 00:40:41,030
Why?

662
00:40:41,760 --> 00:40:43,430
Why is he always like this?

663
00:40:44,070 --> 00:40:46,070
Every time I make up my mind,

664
00:40:48,590 --> 00:40:49,630
he shows up

665
00:40:49,920 --> 00:40:51,800
and undoes everything I've worked so hard for.

666
00:41:19,990 --> 00:41:20,920
Why are you here?

667
00:41:21,430 --> 00:41:22,760
I brought Luke breakfast.

668
00:41:23,030 --> 00:41:23,880
I'll check on him

669
00:41:23,880 --> 00:41:24,800
before heading to the airport.

670
00:41:34,400 --> 00:41:35,110
Luke.

671
00:41:36,030 --> 00:41:36,840
Come here, Luke.

672
00:41:40,400 --> 00:41:41,720
Come, let's not eat bread.

673
00:41:42,550 --> 00:41:43,200
It's not good.

674
00:41:43,200 --> 00:41:43,990
It has no nutrition.

675
00:42:07,510 --> 00:42:09,280
Shang Zhitao, is this how you live?

676
00:42:09,990 --> 00:42:11,470
You don't even have an egg in the fridge.

677
00:42:11,950 --> 00:42:12,680
Mr. Luan,

678
00:42:13,400 --> 00:42:14,510
I don't know how to cook.

679
00:42:15,360 --> 00:42:16,110
Ms. Shang,

680
00:42:16,760 --> 00:42:18,400
you can always learn to cook for yourself.

681
00:42:18,630 --> 00:42:20,150
Why would I learn?

682
00:42:20,630 --> 00:42:21,950
I can order takeout

683
00:42:21,950 --> 00:42:23,680
or eat at my mom's.

684
00:42:24,030 --> 00:42:25,070
Worst case,

685
00:42:25,630 --> 00:42:27,510
I'll find a boyfriend who can cook.

686
00:42:29,990 --> 00:42:31,320
Don't you already have one?

687
00:42:31,720 --> 00:42:32,840
Isn't he your fiancé?

688
00:42:33,550 --> 00:42:34,510
Want me to remind him

689
00:42:34,510 --> 00:42:35,590
to come cook for you?

690
00:42:35,630 --> 00:42:36,800
Tell him

691
00:42:37,030 --> 00:42:38,360
to step up his game.

692
00:42:42,990 --> 00:42:43,800
I'll cook for you.

693
00:42:45,470 --> 00:42:46,400
And for Luke.

694
00:42:49,680 --> 00:42:50,800
I've got to get to work.

695
00:43:05,460 --> 00:43:08,500
♪One look is all it takes to find the right person♪

696
00:43:08,500 --> 00:43:11,340
♪One lifetime is all it takes to commemorate this love♪

697
00:43:12,340 --> 00:43:16,300
♪Whatever remains will be the proof♪

698
00:43:19,580 --> 00:43:22,940
♪If it never crosses your mind♪

699
00:43:22,940 --> 00:43:26,660
♪The tide as I turn back♪

700
00:43:26,660 --> 00:43:30,980
♪Is just formless attraction♪

701
00:43:32,540 --> 00:43:37,860
♪Your silhouette is closing in♪

702
00:43:39,700 --> 00:43:45,300
♪Your breathing grows clear♪

703
00:43:46,860 --> 00:43:51,220
♪Too many distractions in this world♪

704
00:43:51,220 --> 00:43:55,940
♪I would rather forget myself♪

705
00:43:56,220 --> 00:44:00,380
♪Just this moment♪

706
00:44:01,020 --> 00:44:04,420
♪One look is all it takes to find the right person♪

707
00:44:04,420 --> 00:44:07,340
♪One lifetime is all it takes to commemorate this love♪

708
00:44:08,180 --> 00:44:12,380
♪If you miss it, just save the traces♪

709
00:44:15,340 --> 00:44:19,100
♪If your tears fall on their own♪

710
00:44:19,100 --> 00:44:22,420
♪Followed by our hearts beating to the same rhythm♪

711
00:44:22,540 --> 00:44:24,700
♪Will you listen to it♪

712
00:44:24,740 --> 00:44:28,820
♪Or will you reply to me in silence?♪

713
00:44:28,860 --> 00:44:33,780
♪Your silhouette is closing in♪

714
00:44:35,740 --> 00:44:41,940
♪Your breathing grows clear♪

715
00:44:42,740 --> 00:44:47,260
♪Too many distractions in this world♪

716
00:44:47,340 --> 00:44:51,980
♪I would rather forget myself♪

717
00:44:52,060 --> 00:44:57,020
♪All I want is to lose myself in this moment♪

718
00:44:57,340 --> 00:45:03,460
♪Your aloofness masks your vulnerability♪

719
00:45:04,380 --> 00:45:10,540
♪I hide my nervousness in the corner♪

720
00:45:11,620 --> 00:45:16,060
♪Too many hurdles in this world♪

721
00:45:16,100 --> 00:45:20,220
♪Even one moment can keep us warm♪

722
00:45:20,420 --> 00:45:26,220
♪Just this moment♪

723
00:45:26,820 --> 00:45:30,140
♪All right?♪
